Below is what’s happening and how we’ll fix it:

1. Bug scenario & root cause  
   – The user wants to be notified when the multiselect (and dropdown) menu opens or closes, but currently Carbon’s `<MultiSelect>` and `<Dropdown>` only expose an `onChange` (item-selection) callback.  
   – Internally both components manage an `isOpen` state (when you click the toggle or the menu blurs/escapes) but never tell the consumer “hey, the menu just opened/closed.”  
   – We will add a new prop, `onMenuChange({ isOpen })`, to both components, and call it whenever `isOpen` flips.

2. What we change  
   – In `MultiSelect.js`  
     • Add `onMenuChange` to the props signature  
     • Call `onMenuChange({ isOpen: … })` inside the `onStateChange` switch for open/close actions  
     • Declare the new prop in `propTypes` and give it a default of `noop`  
   – In `Dropdown.js`  
     • Import `useEffect` and add `onMenuChange` to the props signature  
     • Use a `useEffect` that watches `isOpen` and fires `onMenuChange({ isOpen })` on every open/close  
     • Declare the new prop in `propTypes` and default it to a no-op  

